From a5bd8fef695fe5eb2926d413c578ee8a7acbb0b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhlport <nhlport@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:29:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] NHL 24: full mip-chain depth/colour copies, AJM
 destroyed-instance jobs, perf stats, RenderDoc trigger

- vk_runtime: CopyImageWithBuffer copies every common mip level through the
  staging buffer instead of level 0 only (the lower levels feed the pre-game
  cutscene blur/DoF chains and were left uninitialised -> noise).
- ajm: a batch job that references an already destroyed decoder instance is
  skipped with a warning instead of asserting (NHL 24 crashed on goal scenes).
- videoout: frame statistics every 5 s (fps, avg/max frame time, frames above
  33/100 ms, pipelines/shaders compiled in the window); pipeline cache counts.
- renderdoc: hotkey uses RenderDoc's present-to-present TriggerCapture and a
  "captures/trigger" file polled by the present thread can start a capture
  without keyboard focus (manual Start/EndFrameCapture never produced a file).
- buffer cache: residency message demoted to debug.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
